        "original_id": "889ddb20-6343-5569-934f-c75eac015767",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. Robert Oppenheimer, Sam Waterston\n- Works: Oppenheimer (miniseries)\n- Organizations: Los Alamos Laboratory, Manhattan Project\n- Events: World War II, atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki\n- Concepts: atomic bomb, nuclear weapons\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, J. Robert Oppenheimer was the wartime head of the Los Alamos Laboratory.\n- During World War II, J. Robert Oppenheimer played a role in the Manhattan Project, the undertaking that developed the first nuclear weapons.\n- J. Robert Oppenheimer is among those credited as the \"father of the atomic bomb\" for his role in the Manhattan Project.\n- The first nuclear weapons developed by the Manhattan Project were used in the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.\n- In the miniseries Oppenheimer, Sam Waterston starred as J. Robert Oppenheimer.",
